#X text 311 355 This can produce some interesting sounds if the different sides get turned on at different times and your ears are in the right state.;
#X text 807 7 This side of the patch accounts for the limits of human hearing. The range of human hearing is about 20Hz to 20kHz. But 20Hz is really quite low. So 40Hz is not a number that can be too hard to hear. Change the number for experimentation with 20Hz. But adding a number after the [random] is needed as you cannot offset with an equation in the [random]. That will push it above 2000 \, so you need to adjust the number to have your regular limit. Use 1960;
