#X text 528 675 You can change the ranges on the different sliders to get different effects. Because all of the sliders produce lower audible frequencies \, you can turn up the (still low) volume on this part of the patch to hear it better. It produces a randomly flucuating beating. Changing the [metro] creation argument also changes things - just things to note.;
#X text 968 668 This part of the patch \, with [metro 1000] kind of gives the output sound kind of a wah-wuh-wah-wuh-wah type effect that reminds of the sound of adults on the Peanuts animated cartoons from TV.;
